<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Silhouette values reached a peak near k = 2, reflecting strong cohesion within a very small number of clusters. However, such a coarse segmentation would provide limited insights into distinct customer behaviours. The score at k = 4 remained reasonably high, striking a balance between cluster separation and practical interpretability. Notably, although k = 3 exhibited slightly higher silhouette value than k = 4, the resulting clusters were less suitable for differentiating meaningful customer segments, as they would create an overly broad grouping in one cluster and reduce business applicability.)
